  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through seven innings until Adames broke it open late.",
    "what_this_means": "McDonald's seven innings of one-run ball gave them a real chance, and the offense finally showed up when it mattered. They left runners on in the first and third. The kind of early waste that usually costs you. But they didn't panic. They stayed in a 1\u20131 game and waited until the eighth, when they scored twice. Adames finished it with a single that made the deficit disappear. This is what the past two wins look like: pitching holds the door, the bats arrive late, the margin stays thin. It works when the reliever doesn't blink and the last swing falls in. They've won twice like this now. That math gets harder.",
